        "original_id": "5d864956-ac6c-575c-a9e5-f091abc4d45a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Margarita Lozano, Luis Buñuel, Sergio Leone, Pier Paolo Pasolini, Paolo and Vittorio Taviani, Nanni Moretti, Claude Berri, Marcel Pagnol\n- Works: Viridiana, A Fistful of Dollars, Pigsty, The Night of the Shooting Stars, Kaos, Good Morning Babylon, La messa è finita, Jean de Florette, Manon of the Spring, Manon des Sources\n- Topics: film collaborations, literary and film adaptation\n\nFacts:\n- Margarita Lozano worked with Luis Buñuel in \"Viridiana,\" Sergio Leone in \"A Fistful of Dollars,\" and Pier Paolo Pasolini in \"Pigsty.\"\n- Margarita Lozano also worked with Paolo and Vittorio Taviani in \"The Night of the Shooting Stars,\" \"Kaos,\" and \"Good Morning Babylon,\" and with Nanni Moretti in \"La messa è finita.\"\n- Margarita Lozano appeared in Claude Berri's two-film project \"Jean de Florette\" and \"Manon of the Spring.\"\n- \"Manon des Sources\" means \"Manon of the Spring\" and is a 1986 French-language film.\n- Claude Berri directed \"Manon des Sources\" as the second of two films adapted from Marcel Pagnol's 1966 two-volume novel.\n- Marcel Pagnol wrote the 1966 two-volume novel underlying \"Manon des Sources\" based on his own earlier film of the same title.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "daf43acb-46fd-5983-94ca-6296f5588a54",
        "text": "Page: Margarita Lozano. Sentence: She has worked for Luis Buñuel in \"Viridiana\", Sergio Leone in \"A Fistful of Dollars\", Pier Paolo Pasolini in \"Pigsty\", the Taviani brothers in \"The Night of the Shooting Stars\", \"Kaos\" and \"Good Morning Babylon\"; Nanni Moretti in \"La messa è finita\"; and in Claude Berri's diptych \"Jean de Florette\" and \"Manon of the Spring\".\nPage: Manon des Sources (1986 film). Sentence: Manon des Sources (] ; meaning Manon of the Spring) is a 1986 French language film.\nPage: Manon des Sources (1986 film). Sentence: Directed by Claude Berri, it is the second of two films adapted from the 1966 two-volume novel by Marcel Pagnol, who wrote it based on his own earlier film of the same title.",
